# More Glider (mapper 30) - continue feature not functioning

- Source URL: https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/NES_MiSTer/issues/435

MiSTer Main: 20250828
NES core: 20251013

More Glider (USA) (Aftermarket) (Unl).nes
CRC32: 4ED588CE

More Glider is an aftermarket NES game released by retroUSB, inspired by a classic shareware game Glider for Macintosh computers. More Glider itself is an updated release of an older aftermarket NES game, called simply Glider (incompatible with the MiSTer core since it uses mapper 29), featuring among other differences multiple new levels. The goal of the game is to navigate a paper airplane across multiple rooms in a house, avoiding other objects or falling to the ground.

The game features a continue feature. Upon running out of lives, player is moved to a simple room containing two chutes on the ceiling, marked as Continue and Reset. Entering the first chute returns player to the previous room in the game, while entering the second chute restarts the game from the first room.

<img width="283" height="242" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aa57ec9a-90a9-4098-a650-e2af5a43e993" />

On the NES core this feature is broken. Entering the Continue chute just restarts this intermediate room, trapping player in a loop with an only exit being exiting through the Reset chute and restarting the game.

The game behaves correctly in Mesen emulator. The game features a battery save feature, remembering the latest room visited and loading it instead of the first room of a house after restarting console. I presume that this may be related to the issue, since the MiSTer core does not appear to save anything during gameplay. Maybe the game fails to write the room id in save memory, and then the continue screen tries to fetch a room to load afterwards from an invalid value?

